    "type": "question",
    "label": "48",
    "prompt": "How many terms of the series $20+18+16+\\cdots$ are needed to give a sum of $104$?",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$8$ terms or $13$ terms.",
      "worked": "$a=20$, $d=18-20=-2$ and $S_n=104$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}S_n&=\\frac{n}{2}[2a+(n-1)d]\\\\104&=\\frac{n}{2}[2(20)+(n-1)(-2)]\\\\208&=n[40-2n+2]\\\\208&=n(42-2n)\\\\208&=42n-2n^2\\\\2n^2-42n+208&=0\\\\n^2-21n+104&=0\\\\(n-13)(n-8)&=0\\\\n&=13\\text{ or }8.\\end{align*}$$\n\nTherefore, $8$ terms or $13$ terms are needed.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
